<p>(A) -- Supplemental pro forma earnings data gives effect to (a) the March 6, 1997, initial public offering of common stock and companion offerings of senior debt and trust preferred securities, and (b) the special dividends paid by NFS, as if the transactions had occurred at the beginning of each year presented.  Accordingly, in each period presented, pro forma earnings data give effect to interest expense associated with the senior debt and trust preferred securities, assumed investment income foregone on the special dividend to Nationwide Mutual and investment income assumed on the proceeds from the debt and equity offerings.</p>
<p>(B) -- Pro forma weighted average shares outstanding gives effect to the March 6, 1997, initial public offering of common stock, which includes 23.6 million Class A common shares issued in the initial public offering and subsequent underwriters' overallotment, and 104.8 million Class B common shares held by Nationwide Mutual.</p>
<p>(C) -- Net operating income excludes from net income after-tax realized investment gains and losses and income from discontinued operations. Nationwide Financial Services, Inc.</p>
